# Unit Tests (Clean Code Ch.9)

Expo’s unit-test story is **Jest** via `jest-expo` (SDK 58 needs Jest 30) and `@testing-library/react-native` for components. Prefer `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` in this repo.

## FIRST

Fast, Independent, Repeatable, Self-validating, Timely.

## AAA

Arrange / Act / Assert. One concept per test. Names say behavior (`matchStatus returns live inside the live window`).

## Dual standard

Production size/complexity gates stay strict. Spec, `*.test`, harness, and `__tests__` files may relax max-lines / complexity / max-classes — keep naming and “no empty catch” discipline.

## Harness / DSL

Put fixture clocks (`now`), sample `Match` builders, and stub catalogs in `*.harness.ts` (or `__tests__/helpers`) — not inline in every `it`. Shared fixtures live in `modules/shared/shared.harness.ts`. Prefer `rejects.toThrow` / RNTL queries over try/catch for expected failures. Feature Presenter / use-case logic under `modules/features/` should be unit-tested without rendering Views. Presenter hooks use `await renderHook` from `@testing-library/react-native` (RNTL 14 is async). Mock `./router` with a factory (`jest.fn`) so Jest never loads `expo-router`. Use-case tests pass fixture entities — they must not import `data/` sample catalogs.

## Coverage

Prefer meaningful tests over chasing percentage alone. Run `npm run test:coverage` for a report under `coverage/` (gitignored). Collection covers use cases / Presenter / `lib/format-time` and `data/`, excluding Views, contracts, entities, gateways, harnesses, and specs.
